# Manuscript. Drafts, figures, LaTeX build and the Overleaf bundle live outside version
# control; the paper is authored elsewhere and assembled from this repo's scripts.
#
# The pattern is `paper/*`, not `paper/`, because git cannot re-include a file under a
# directory that is itself excluded, and one file has to be re-included: references.bib
# is not a draft. Every entry in it carries the note recording what was checked against
# an authoritative record and what was not, and manuscript 6.2 names it as one of the
# two places the provenance audit is documented. A reader sent to a file that is not in
# the repository is the failure this paper reports on.
paper/*
!paper/references.bib

# Rendered page images of the manuscript
tmp/

# OS and interpreter junk
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Session transcripts. These are working records of assistant sessions, not project
# artefacts: they contain unedited intermediate reasoning, dead ends and draft text that
# the deviation log and vault/log.md record properly. Keeping them out of a public
# repository is deliberate.
*-local-command-caveat*.txt
